or something ridiculous.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.110
It sounds absurd, but it's
probably worth that much, right?

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:40.900
So clearly these guys have
big bucks to spend around.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:43.330
- I mean, I'm just glad
a company is giving

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.037
the power back to the people
(Joey laughs)

00:02:45.037 --> 00:02:47.571
and taking on small indie
companies like Sony.

00:02:47.571 --> 00:02:48.987
- Fuck license holders, man!

00:02:48.987 --> 00:02:52.955
- Taking on small indie
companies like Sony and AT&amp;T.

00:02:52.955 --> 00:02:55.620
You know, someone's gotta
take these indie companies

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.453
out of the field.
- What were they gonna do?

00:02:56.453 --> 00:02:57.286
What were they gonna do with it?

00:02:57.286 --> 00:02:59.540
So essentially this
Kickstarter promised that

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:03.160
and it raised in one day like $110,000.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.760
- Which is absurd.
- It literally came out of

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.140
nowhere because I remember we were,

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.320
