00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.750
But you could, they could just pirate it,

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.850
if they really want to
really get it for free.

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:47.440
I'm not saying you should. I
condone that, do not do it.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.273
But...

00:06:48.273 --> 00:06:49.621
if you're gonna

00:06:49.621 --> 00:06:51.813
(Connor blubbers)

00:06:51.813 --> 00:06:52.646
- I mean, it's also like,

00:06:52.646 --> 00:06:55.130
with the money that they
gave to this Kickstarter,

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:57.200
because there were a lot
of people who were giving

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.620
hundreds of dollars to this Kickstarter.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.660
And some people I saw
were giving literally

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:03.368
thousands of dollars to this Kickstarter.

00:07:03.368 --> 00:07:05.710
- When I looked, there
was a thousand backers

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.820
giving a hundred thousand, so.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.500
- Rough, on average, a
hundred dollars each, right.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:10.333
- They're giving a lot of money to this--

00:07:10.333 --> 00:07:14.250
- That's like a year's
subscription to Netflix

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:15.578
or Crunchyroll or any of them.

00:07:15.578 --> 00:07:16.411
- It's not about the money, Joey!

00:07:16.411 --> 00:07:18.390
It's about the message I'm sending.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:20.437
- It's about sending a
message, the message of

00:07:20.437 --> 00:07:22.280
"I got scammed."

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:23.240
- I mean, it's the,

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:24.830
it's the thing is where,

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:27.949
if anyone just literally
used a single brain cell,

00:07:27.949 --> 00:07:31.350
to think about the logistics of this--

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.210
- The logistics!

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:35.420
