a part of me that hears that
kind of stuff happening,

00:52:47.340 --> 00:52:49.910
and just makes me wish
that young people in Japan

00:52:49.910 --> 00:52:52.200
were a little more politically interested.

00:52:52.200 --> 00:52:54.320
- Yeah, they pretty much have no interest

00:52:54.320 --> 00:52:56.318
or even if they do, they
don't talk about it publicly.

00:52:56.318 --> 00:52:58.700
- No, no. No one talks about it publicly.

00:52:58.700 --> 00:52:59.940
Barely anyone has any interest.

00:52:59.940 --> 00:53:01.625
No one believes in the government here.

00:53:01.625 --> 00:53:02.458
They're just like,

00:53:02.458 --> 00:53:03.780
"Yeah, whatever. They're
just doing their thing.

00:53:03.780 --> 00:53:06.120
As long as we're not in a war
with another country, we good.

00:53:06.120 --> 00:53:07.090
- The consensus seems to be,

00:53:07.090 --> 00:53:08.119
from when I've spoke to people,

00:53:08.119 --> 00:53:09.380
is that they're like, "Oh, I don't care.

00:53:09.380 --> 00:53:10.713
As long as they don't ruin my life."

00:53:10.713 --> 00:53:11.546
- There's a lot of young people

00:53:11.546 --> 00:53:13.080
who don't even know who
the prime minister is.

00:53:13.080 --> 00:53:14.230
- Wow.

00:53:14.230 --> 00:53:16.130
- It just goes to show
they're that out of touch.

00:53:16.130 --> 00:53:19.410
- But in Japan, you don't get
to choose the prime minister.

00:53:19.410 --> 00:53:20.570
- No.
- You choose the party.

00:53:20.570 --> 00:53:22.240
And then they choose the prime minister.

00:53:22.240 --> 00:53:23.073
Whereas, you know,

00:53:23.073 --> 00:53:24.610
I think that's technically
the same in the UK,

00:53:24.610 --> 00:53:25.990
but it's not done like that at all.

00:53:25.990 --> 00:53:27.658
We're promised who the
person is when we're voting.

00:53:27.658 --> 00:53:28.491
And that's how it is.

00:53:28.491 --> 00:53:30.127
But in Japan, you vote for the party

00:53:30.127 --> 00:53:32.000
and you don't get a say who they pick.

00:53:32.000 --> 00:53:33.590
- But, again, it's like,
I've talked to young people,

00:53:33.590 --> 00:53:34.423
you know,

00:53:34.423 --> 00:53:35.830
some same age, a little bit
older, a little bit younger.

00:53:35.830 --> 00:53:37.240
And there's a lot of
them who don't even know

00:53:37.240 --> 00:53:38.923
what the political parties
are or what they do.

00:53:38.923 --> 00:53:41.770
They're just not interested
in it whatsoever.

00:53:41.770 --> 00:53:42.603
And it's like--

00:53:42.603 --> 00:53:45.130
- I kind of get the vibe
that everyone is just like

00:53:45.130 --> 00:53:46.320
so overworked.

00:53:46.320 --> 00:53:48.430
They don't have time to care.

00:53:48.430 --> 00:53:50.460
- It's the last thing
they wanna worry about.

00:53:50.460 --> 00:53:52.580
- That's pretty much
the vibe I get, is like

00:53:52.580 --> 00:53:55.750
everyone's just fucking fighting
for their life as it is.

00:53:55.750 --> 00:53:57.120
Everyone's just trying
to get through the day.

00:53:57.120 --> 00:54:00.590
They don't have time to
care about other issues,

00:54:00.590 --> 00:54:01.787
a lot of the time.

00:54:01.787 --> 00:54:06.787
- I remember when they
raised the GST from 8% to 10%

00:54:06.840 --> 00:54:09.440
and there was all these mobs.

00:54:09.440 --> 00:54:10.273
- I saw that.

00:54:10.273 --> 00:54:11.827
- All these mobs of all
these old people being like,

00:54:11.827 --> 00:54:13.190
"How fucking dare you?"

00:54:13.190 --> 00:54:14.407
Meanwhile, the young people are like,

00:54:14.407 --> 00:54:17.630
"Understandable, have a nice
day, I'll just work harder."

00:54:17.630 --> 00:54:19.130
It's like, they just don't care.

00:54:19.130 --> 00:54:21.220
It's like, "Oh, they made a new law?

00:54:21.220 --> 00:54:22.670
Sick. I guess I'm just gonna have to

00:54:22.670 --> 00:54:24.993
mold my life around this new law, now.

00:54:26.659 --> 00:54:27.960
- Speaking of dumb Japanese laws,

00:54:27.960 --> 00:54:32.960
you can be arrested in
Japan if you mod games,

00:54:33.320 --> 00:54:35.000
like save files.

00:54:35.000 --> 00:54:36.927
- Yeah, that sounds about right.

00:54:36.927 --> 00:54:38.660
- Can you actually?

00:54:38.660 --> 00:54:39.493
- A guy in--

00:54:39.493 --> 00:54:41.704
- The Skyrim community
are sweating right now.

00:54:41.704 --> 00:54:42.537
(Joey and Garnt laugh)

00:54:42.537 --> 00:54:45.300
- A guy in Nagano, I think,

00:54:45.300 --> 00:54:50.070
was arrested and fined 65,000 pounds,

00:54:50.070 --> 00:54:53.250
about $100K in dollars,

00:54:53.250 --> 00:54:56.513
for selling Breath of the Wild
save files that were modded.

00:54:57.660 --> 00:54:58.720
- Seriously?

00:54:58.720 --> 00:55:00.020
- Yeah, no joke.

00:55:00.020 --> 00:55:01.490
And apparently, like I've read about it.

00:55:01.490 --> 00:55:03.980
Apparently, one of the main
reasons why this law was passed

00:55:03.980 --> 00:55:05.400
was because,

00:55:05.400 --> 00:55:07.580
guess which company pushed for it.

00:55:07.580 --> 00:55:08.650
- Nintendo.
- Yeah!

00:55:08.650 --> 00:55:10.400
- Of course they did.

00:55:11.300 --> 00:55:12.450
- But obviously they tried,

00:55:12.450 --> 00:55:13.560
obviously that shit just,

00:55:13.560 --> 00:55:15.140
America's like, "LMAO, no."

00:55:15.140 --> 00:55:17.254
They're not passing that law in America

00:55:17.254 --> 00:55:18.535
because you have the right
to do whatever you want

00:55:18.535 --> 00:55:20.280
with the products you buy.

00:55:20.280 --> 00:55:23.510
But yeah, Nintendo somehow
managed to push for a law.

00:55:23.510 --> 00:55:27.010
- To be fair, I think the
selling part was the problem.

00:55:27.010 --> 00:55:28.140
If you just put it online--

00:55:28.140 --> 00:55:31.686
- But it's also illegal to
even mod a Switch in Japan.

00:55:31.686 --> 00:55:32.857
You can't mod a Switch in Japan.

00:55:32.857 --> 00:55:33.893
- But I think it was
extra bad for the dude

00:55:33.893 --> 00:55:35.190
because he sold it for money.

00:55:35.190 --> 00:55:37.390
- I mean, isn't it technically illegal

00:55:37.390 --> 00:55:39.530
everywhere to mod a Switch?

00:55:39.530 --> 00:55:40.363
- No, no, no.

00:55:40.363 --> 00:55:41.196
So, in the U.S.,

00:55:42.440 --> 00:55:44.380
it's counted as you bought a product,

00:55:44.380 --> 00:55:45.430
and you're allowed to do whatever you want

00:55:45.430 --> 00:55:46.543
with that product.

00:55:46.543 --> 00:55:47.487
You can do whatever you want.

00:55:47.487 --> 00:55:49.090
- So what's the illegal part, then?

00:55:49.090 --> 00:55:50.780
Buying the games, getting the games?

00:55:50.780 --> 00:55:51.620
- Apparently.

00:55:51.620 --> 00:55:54.280
So I think the way they've
managed to pass the law is that

00:55:54.280 --> 00:55:57.020
it's still an ongoing
thing, like a service.

00:55:57.020 --> 00:55:58.707
You don't actually own the game.

00:55:58.707 --> 00:56:00.460
You own a copy of the game.

00:56:00.460 --> 00:56:02.897
And by changing it, you're
ruining or infringing--

00:56:02.897 --> 00:56:06.660
- If you buy a Nintendo
product, Nintendo owns you.

00:56:06.660 --> 00:56:07.667
There is no escape.

00:56:09.310 --> 00:56:10.530
- Didn't Apple try--

00:56:10.530 --> 00:56:12.620
I don't know if it's illegal, again,

00:56:12.620 --> 00:56:14.696
can you check it if it's
illegal to jailbreak your phone?

00:56:14.696 --> 00:56:15.650
I can't remember.

00:56:15.650 --> 00:56:17.510
I'm pretty sure it's not--

00:56:17.510 --> 00:56:18.590
- I think it is illegal.
- I think it is.

00:56:18.590 --> 00:56:19.510
- In every country?

00:56:19.510 --> 00:56:23.106
- I don't know. Is it, or
does it just break warranty?

00:56:23.106 --> 00:56:24.930
- I thought it just
broke warranty in the UK.

00:56:24.930 --> 00:56:26.087
I can't remember though.

00:56:26.087 --> 00:56:28.319
- [Man] It definitely at
least breaks warranty.

00:56:28.319 --> 00:56:29.500
- I know that.

00:56:29.500 --> 00:56:31.040
- Everyone knows that.

00:56:31.040 --> 00:56:31.873
- Generally, you're allowed
to do what the fuck you want

00:56:31.873 --> 00:56:32.980
with the stuff you own.

00:56:32.980 --> 00:56:35.080
- I've never hard of
anyone getting arrested

00:56:35.080 --> 00:56:36.970
for jailbreaking their phone.

00:56:36.970 --> 00:56:41.750
- Just the idea of a raid
going on into some guy's house.

00:56:41.750 --> 00:56:46.230
Like, "Get down! Stop! Drop
the Legend of Zelda copies!

00:56:46.230 --> 00:56:47.380
Put them on the floor!"

00:56:49.030 --> 00:56:49.925
You know, in Japan,

00:56:49.925 --> 00:56:51.130
The thing is in Japan, right--

00:56:51.130 --> 00:56:52.410
- Boys walk up with hazmat suits.

00:56:52.410 --> 00:56:54.200
- When they arrest people in Japan,

00:56:54.200 --> 00:56:55.750
they don't arrest you with two people.

00:56:55.750 --> 00:56:58.000
They send like twenty fucking
police officers, in Japan,

00:56:58.000 --> 00:56:58.870
when they arrest you.

00:56:58.870 --> 00:57:00.100
- The send the boys down, man.

00:57:00.100 --> 00:57:01.700
They got the whole squad coming.

00:57:02.740 --> 00:57:06.251
- [Navi] Overall, it's breaking
your iPhone's warranty.

00:57:06.251 --> 00:57:09.170
The legality, I think it
differs between the country.

00:57:09.170 --> 00:57:11.763
But in terms of Apple,
it's like, you don't get--

00:57:11.763 --> 00:57:13.971
- No, no, no, yeah.

00:57:13.971 --> 00:57:15.257
They're not gonna fucking
sue you for doing it.

00:57:15.257 --> 00:57:17.457
- [Navi] So, it's just
your warranty's gone.

00:57:18.460 --> 00:57:19.416
- I mean, that's understandable.

00:57:19.416 --> 00:57:20.249
- Most products do that.

00:57:20.249 --> 00:57:21.860
Like, "Hey, if you change this thing,

00:57:21.860 --> 00:57:22.693
we're not gonna fix it for you."

00:57:22.693 --> 00:57:24.396
- If you break the seal that says,

00:57:24.396 --> 00:57:26.600
"Breaking the seal breaks the warranty,"

00:57:26.600 --> 00:57:29.133
then generally, that
breaks the warranty, right?

00:57:30.030 --> 00:57:31.110
- Yeah, but then I feel, you know,

00:57:31.110 --> 00:57:33.230
you also have to understand that Japan

00:57:33.230 --> 00:57:37.510
is falling a little bit short
on most common sense laws,

00:57:37.510 --> 00:57:40.370
like Fair Use, for example.

00:57:40.370 --> 00:57:41.390
- Fair Use just isn't a thing here,

00:57:41.390 --> 00:57:42.670
as we've found out many times.

00:57:42.670 --> 00:57:45.210
- Just seeing all these
videos of Nintendo fans

00:57:45.210 --> 00:57:47.450
pleading with Nintendo
to change their mind.

00:57:47.450 --> 00:57:49.510
And then, after living
here, I'm like, dude, it's--

00:57:49.510 --> 00:57:50.970
- It's not gonna happen.

00:57:50.970 --> 00:57:52.500
- That's not how it rolls.

00:57:52.500 --> 00:57:54.330
It's like, us pleading with Nintendo

00:57:54.330 --> 00:57:55.910
is not gonna fucking do
anything unless you're--

00:57:55.910 --> 00:57:58.217
- We should start a Kickstarter

00:57:58.217 --> 00:58:00.113
to get them to change the laws!

00:58:01.223 --> 00:58:04.170
- Unless you are fully
100% Japanese and in that

00:58:04.170 --> 00:58:06.580
boardroom meeting with
them, isn't going to matter.

00:58:06.580 --> 00:58:09.480
- Unless you're Shigeru
Miyamoto, it's not gonna change.

00:58:09.480 --> 00:58:11.480
- Yeah, definitely coming to live here

00:58:11.480 --> 00:58:13.240
and seeing how it works on the inside,

00:58:13.240 --> 00:58:15.166
I'm just like, yeah, it's a lot of,

00:58:15.166 --> 00:58:17.950
no matter how much noise
gets made on Twitter,

00:58:17.950 --> 00:58:20.190
I think most of the time it's
going to fall on deaf ears.

00:58:20.190 --> 00:58:23.290
- Yeah, so the way that
I've come to realize,

00:58:23.290 --> 00:58:24.640
at least from living here,

00:58:24.640 --> 00:58:26.550
you can say anything
you want over an email.

00:58:26.550 --> 00:58:28.210
You can explain everything
as well as you want

00:58:28.210 --> 00:58:29.043
through a different person.

00:58:29.043 --> 00:58:32.770
But unless there is a
Japanese guy there in the room

00:58:32.770 --> 00:58:33.603
at the board meeting,

00:58:33.603 --> 00:58:35.570
explaining something
directly to the person,

00:58:35.570 --> 00:58:36.403
it will not get changed.

00:58:36.403 --> 00:58:38.850
- You can't have a Zoom call,
you can't send an email,

00:58:38.850 --> 00:58:40.992
you can't send an angry tweet.

00:58:40.992 --> 00:58:43.910
You know, you could fucking
ratio the shit out of Nintendo,

00:58:43.910 --> 00:58:46.230
they'll be like, "I don't give a shit."

00:58:46.230 --> 00:58:49.340
You need to have someone there
explaining to the person,

00:58:49.340 --> 00:58:51.620
in person, speaking fluent Japanese,

00:58:51.620 --> 00:58:53.730
and possibly having a Japanese passport,

00:58:53.730 --> 00:58:55.830
before they take anything seriously.

00:58:55.830 --> 00:58:57.843
- Even then it's like, "Oh, so
what company do you work for?

00:58:57.843 --> 00:59:00.800
Who are your backers? Who
are you representing?"

00:59:00.800 --> 00:59:03.280
- I've worked at places where
I've wanted to shoot there,

00:59:03.280 --> 00:59:05.317
And I've had a friend tell
them, who wasn't Japanese,

00:59:05.317 --> 00:59:06.427
"Hey, can we shoot
there? And they're like,

00:59:06.427 --> 00:59:07.440
"No, I don't know about it."

00:59:07.440 --> 00:59:09.620
But then you have a Japanese
person do the exact same thing,

00:59:09.620 --> 00:59:11.357
like if Kaho hits them up and is like,

00:59:11.357 --> 00:59:12.366
"Hey, this is what we're doing."

00:59:12.366 --> 00:59:13.740
And they're like, "Oh, okay, sure."

00:59:13.740 --> 00:59:15.780
It's like, what?

00:59:15.780 --> 00:59:17.540
It's just they don't believe you.

00:59:17.540 --> 00:59:19.210
They think you're lying
'cause you're not Japanese.

00:59:19.210 --> 00:59:20.680
Like you don't understand. You
don't understand how I think.

00:59:20.680 --> 00:59:23.700
- These sneaky foreigners
trying to get around our ways.

00:59:23.700 --> 00:59:26.090
- It's bizarre. It's really strange.

00:59:26.090 --> 00:59:28.160
But that's just the way that it's,

00:59:28.160 --> 00:59:29.820
businesses is done here.

00:59:29.820 --> 00:59:30.861
And it's, you know,

00:59:30.861 --> 00:59:35.520
it makes so much sense now
why these companies do this

00:59:35.520 --> 00:59:37.080
fucking stupid shit.

00:59:37.080 --> 00:59:38.100
I'm like, oh, I totally get it now.

00:59:38.100 --> 00:59:41.290
- And I'm kind of like sitting
in that halfway point, right?

00:59:41.290 --> 00:59:43.157
'Cause if I don't open
my mouth, they'll be like

00:59:43.157 --> 00:59:45.590
"This fucking foreigner
tryna get around me."

00:59:45.590 --> 00:59:46.857
The moment I open my mouth, they're like,

00:59:46.857 --> 00:59:49.457
"Oh, you're Nihongo? Nihongo Jouzu?

00:59:49.457 --> 00:59:50.963
All right, let's do it, boys."

00:59:50.963 --> 00:59:53.570
- All right, let's do business, right?

00:59:53.570 --> 00:59:55.587
- Exactly. I rock up, let's do business.

00:59:55.587 --> 00:59:56.820
"No, you're a foreigner."

00:59:56.820 --> 00:59:58.580
JK, I am Nihongo Jouzu actually.

00:59:58.580 --> 00:59:59.800
And they're like, "All right, I'm sorry.

00:59:59.800 --> 01:00:01.330
All right. Let's do some business."

01:00:01.330 --> 01:00:04.483
I'm like, it's so fucking embarrassing.

01:00:05.736 --> 01:00:09.740
- Yeah. And I feel like companies
in Japan are very, very,

01:00:09.740 --> 01:00:11.410
what's the word?

01:00:11.410 --> 01:00:14.320
They very much stick to
the hierarchy of decisions.

01:00:14.320 --> 01:00:16.880
And if you're not

01:00:16.880 --> 01:00:19.530
the same level, you can't comment.

01:00:19.530 --> 01:00:22.185
- Are you talking about the pyramid?

01:00:22.185 --> 01:00:23.018
- The pyramid scheme.

01:00:23.018 --> 01:00:24.050
- The pyramid scheme.

01:00:24.050 --> 01:00:26.969
- Well, if you're not in that meeting,

01:00:26.969 --> 01:00:29.580
your opinion doesn't matter
no matter who you talk to.

01:00:29.580 --> 01:00:31.110
So I feel like when people
are like, all right,

01:00:31.110 --> 01:00:32.270
even if like, I don't know,

01:00:32.270 --> 01:00:33.850
because Nintendo has
a Nintendo of America.

01:00:33.850 --> 01:00:36.160
I'd love to know how
much Nintendo of America

01:00:36.160 --> 01:00:38.660
has a say over what
Nintendo, the Japan office,

01:00:38.660 --> 01:00:39.493
I feel like--

01:00:39.493 --> 01:00:40.326
- Probably not a lot.

01:00:40.326 --> 01:00:41.240
I feel like people would,

01:00:41.240 --> 01:00:42.620
yeah, I think it's probably not a lot.

01:00:42.620 --> 01:00:45.130
Just based off like what I've
seen from other companies here

01:00:45.130 --> 01:00:46.870
where you would think that
they would have an input,

01:00:46.870 --> 01:00:48.040
but they don't.

01:00:48.040 --> 01:00:49.737
- Doug Bowser is like,

01:00:49.737 --> 01:00:51.026
"So can we change this thing?"

01:00:51.026 --> 01:00:53.470
And they're like, "But
we're in a Zoom call.

01:00:53.470 --> 01:00:56.350
You're not in the office.
So, I don't know about that."

01:00:56.350 --> 01:00:57.520
- Again, it's all speculation,

01:00:57.520 --> 01:01:00.160
but I imagine it's, if any,
from what I've seen here,

01:01:00.160 --> 01:01:02.000
it's very difficult to get things done

01:01:02.000 --> 01:01:02.953
if you're not the same level.

01:01:02.953 --> 01:01:04.940
- Basically, the longer I live in Japan,

01:01:04.940 --> 01:01:08.852
the more respect I have
for Suzaku in Code Geass.

01:01:08.852 --> 01:01:10.390
'Cause you watch Code Geass

01:01:10.390 --> 01:01:12.170
and everyone wants to
be the Lelouch, right.

01:01:12.170 --> 01:01:14.680
Everyone wants to be the fucking Lelouch.

01:01:14.680 --> 01:01:17.260
Bring down the system,
fuck the corporations.

01:01:17.260 --> 01:01:18.093
But then I'm just like,

01:01:18.093 --> 01:01:20.540
yo, Suzaku's out there
working his fucking ass off

01:01:20.540 --> 01:01:22.390
to change shit, man.

01:01:22.390 --> 01:01:24.680
He's the real one. He's the real one.

01:01:24.680 --> 01:01:25.866
- He's climbing that pyramid, boys.

01:01:25.866 --> 01:01:27.500
- He's climbing the hierarchy, man.

01:01:27.500 --> 01:01:31.477
- If this was IRL, Suzaku would
still be a fucking grunt--

01:01:31.477 --> 01:01:34.760
(Garnt laughs)

01:01:34.760 --> 01:01:36.370
He's like, "Well, what
do you mean, you're 22?

01:01:36.370 --> 01:01:37.697
No permission for you."

01:01:37.697 --> 01:01:40.237
- "Do you have work experience?
Then stay the fuck down."

01:01:40.237 --> 01:01:42.160
- "Oh, you're an honorary Britannian?

01:01:42.160 --> 01:01:45.885
No, no. What the fuck is
an honorary Britannian?

01:01:45.885 --> 01:01:46.718
You're not one of the--"

01:01:46.718 --> 01:01:49.041
- Oh, yeah, he wasn't even one of them.

01:01:49.041 --> 01:01:51.600
There's no way he could pass. No, no, no.

01:01:51.600 --> 01:01:54.310
He's the guy who changes
the vending machines.

